IMPORT prelude

-- Singapore Totalisator Board Act 1987 (Singapore) -- what a totalisator agency must pay out to punters and what it keeps
-- (ss 15, 16), what the Board may and may not do (ss 4(1), 4(4), 5(1), 9(2)), admission to race courses and turf club by-laws
-- (s 17), the Board's financial year (s 14), and who may sit on the Board and how it decides (s 7(1); Schedule paras 8, 10, 12(2), (3)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/STBA1987.txt. The deposit
-- says the revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on
-- 31 December 2021", and is marked "Informal Consolidation -- version in force from 1/8/2022"; the latest amendment annotated in
-- the body is Act 14 of 2022 wef 01/08/2022 (Act 1 of 2022 wef 29/07/2022 for s 15(1)(a)). The meta file records the version as
-- current at 1 October 2026. The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is out of step with the body (it lists ss 17
-- to 20 as repealed and "General exemption" as s 21); this encoding follows the body, where admission to race courses is s 17,
-- ss 18 to 22 are repealed, the exemption is s 23, regulations s 24 and the Turf Club trust s 25.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0147 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl): Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. For a punter that is the dividend rule; for a racegoer, admission and removal; for a turf club or agency, the
-- by-law publication duty and the Board's supervisory powers. Not encoded: incorporation (s 3), s 4(2), (3) and s 6 ministerial
-- directions and information, the chief executive and officers (ss 8, 9(1)), bank accounts, investment, shares and borrowing
-- (ss 10 to 13), the s 23 exemption and s 24 regulations (the commission rates themselves are in regulations not retrieved), the
-- Turf Club trust (s 25), and Schedule paras 1 to 7, 9, 11, 12(1), (4) to (6) and 13 to 15. The Gambling Duties Act 2022 was not read, so gambling duty
-- is an input.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions as shown in the example rows. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Singapore Totalisator Board Act 1987 -- racing and totalisators`

§§ `15 and 16 -- the dividend, and what the Board keeps`

-- s 15(1): "It is the duty of every totalisator agency operating a totalisator to pay out by way of dividend all moneys received
-- from investments on the totalisator after deducting -- (a) the amount of any gambling duty charged under the Gambling Duties
-- Act 2022; and (b) the amount of any commission prescribed ... in any regulations made under section 24."
-- (2): "It is not necessary to pay out fractions of a dollar."
-- s 16: the commission, "together with any fractional money arising pursuant to the operation of section 15(2), are deemed for
-- all purposes to belong to and form part of the general funds of the Board and may be apportioned between the Board and the
-- totalisator agency in such proportion and in such manner as the Minister may approve."
--
-- Reading (inference): s 15(2) is applied to the pool as a whole -- the agency complies if it pays out the net pool, or the net pool
-- less something under a dollar. The text does not say whether fractions are dropped per ticket or per pool.
GIVEN `money received` IS A NUMBER, `gambling duty` IS A NUMBER, `commission` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dividend pool` MEANS
    `money received` MINUS `gambling duty` MINUS `commission`

GIVEN `money received` IS A NUMBER, `gambling duty` IS A NUMBER, `commission` IS A NUMBER, `amount paid out` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agency has paid out as s 15 requires` IF
        `amount paid out` AT MOST `the dividend pool` `money received` `gambling duty` `commission`
    AND `the dividend pool` `money received` `gambling duty` `commission` MINUS `amount paid out` LESS THAN 1

GIVEN `money received` IS A NUMBER, `gambling duty` IS A NUMBER, `commission` IS A NUMBER, `amount paid out` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum belonging to the Board's general funds` MEANS
    `commission` PLUS (`the dividend pool` `money received` `gambling duty` `commission` MINUS `amount paid out`)

§§ `4(1), 4(4), 5(1) and 9(2) -- what the Board may do`

-- s 4(1): functions include "(a) to supervise the affairs of a turf club operating in Singapore"; (b) equine research and training
-- centres; "(d) with the approval of the Minister, to establish and maintain places and facilities for recreation on land owned
-- or held by the Board"; "(f) to work collaboratively with the Gambling Regulatory Authority of Singapore to foster responsible
-- gambling".
-- s 4(4): "However, nothing in this Act confers on the Board a function or power to conduct on its own behalf any race meeting or
-- a totalisator for gaming in relation to any racing or otherwise."
-- s 5(1)(c): power "to suspend or revoke any totalisator or gaming activity established by any totalisator agency under the
-- supervision of the Board".
-- s 9(1)(b): the Board may appoint totalisator agencies; (2): "The Board must obtain the approval of the Minister for the
-- appointment of -- ... (b) any totalisator agency."
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `supervising a turf club`
    `conducting equine research`
    `fostering responsible gambling with the Gambling Regulatory Authority`
    `suspending a totalisator agency's gaming activity`
    `opening a recreation facility on Board land`
    `appointing a totalisator agency`
    `conducting a race meeting on its own behalf`
    `running a totalisator on its own behalf`

GIVEN `the activity` IS A Activity, `the Minister has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may carry on the activity` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `conducting a race meeting on its own behalf` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `running a totalisator on its own behalf` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `opening a recreation facility on Board land` THEN `the Minister has approved`
    WHEN `appointing a totalisator agency` THEN `the Minister has approved`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 4A: the Board ensures "public benefits may be derived from any racing or gaming ... through regular contributions out of their
-- proceeds or profits so as to fund distributions under section 5".
-- s 5(1)(a): power "to distribute sums, out of moneys forming part of the funds of the Board and not required by it in the exercise
-- of its functions under section 4, for ... (i) public, social or charitable purposes relating to Singapore; (ii) the promotion of
-- culture, art and sport generally in Singapore".
-- Reading (inference): a purpose with no relation to Singapore, such as an overseas appeal, falls outside both limbs.
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `a Singapore charity`
    `a Singapore community project`
    `promoting sport in Singapore`
    `promoting the arts in Singapore`
    `an overseas relief appeal`
    `promoting a foreign arts festival abroad`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purpose is one s 5(1)(a) allows` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `an overseas relief appeal` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `promoting a foreign arts festival abroad` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose, `the money is required for the Board's s 4 functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may distribute the money` IF
    `the purpose is one s 5(1)(a) allows` `the purpose` AND (NOT `the money is required for the Board's s 4 functions`)

§§ `17 -- admission to race courses and turf club by-laws`

-- s 17(1): "A turf club may admit members of the public to any race course or premises under the control or supervision of the
-- club ... on payment of an admission fee." (2), (3): by-laws may control admission and may exclude "any specified class or
-- description of persons, either absolutely or subject to the conditions prescribed". (4)(a): the section applies "despite the fact
-- that it is or forms part of a reserve or other place in respect of which there exists a right of public use or entry".
-- (5): "An officer of the turf club may remove from the race course or such premises any person who contravenes any by-law made
-- under this section and who fails or refuses to leave the race course or such premises after being requested by such officer to
-- do so."
GIVEN `the race course carries a public right of entry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the turf club may charge for admission` IF
    TRUE

GIVEN `contravened a by-law` IS A BOOLEAN, `was asked to leave by an officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `failed or refused to leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an officer may remove the person under s 17(5)` IF
    `contravened a by-law` AND `was asked to leave by an officer` AND `failed or refused to leave`

-- s 17(6): every by-law or amendment "must, within 30 days of its coming into operation -- (a) be published on the website of the
-- Singapore Turf Club (the publication cost of which must be borne by the turf club ...); and (b) be displayed prominently within
-- the premises of the turf club."
-- (7): a by-law inconsistent "with any law for the time being in force in Singapore ... is, to the extent of the inconsistency,
-- void."
GIVEN `days to website publication` IS A NUMBER, `days to display on premises` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the by-law was published as s 17(6) requires` IF
    `days to website publication` AT MOST 30 AND `days to display on premises` AT MOST 30

GIVEN `the by-law is inconsistent with Singapore law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the by-law is effective` IF
    NOT `the by-law is inconsistent with Singapore law`

§§ `14 -- financial year`

-- s 14: "The financial year of the Board begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year."
-- The result is the calendar year in which the financial year containing the given month began.
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER, `month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year the Board's financial year began` MEANS
    IF `month` AT LEAST 4 THEN `calendar year` ELSE `calendar year` MINUS 1

§§ `7(1) and the Schedule -- the Board`

-- s 7(1): the Board consists of "(a) a Chairperson; and (b) not less than 4 and not more than 11 other members as the Minister may
-- determine."
GIVEN `there is a Chairperson` IS A BOOLEAN, `number of other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board's composition fits s 7(1)` IF
    `there is a Chairperson` AND `number of other members` AT LEAST 4 AND `number of other members` AT MOST 11

-- Schedule para 10: a person "must not be appointed or continue to hold office as a member if he or she -- (a) is an undischarged
-- bankrupt or has made any arrangement with his or her creditors; or (b) has been sentenced to imprisonment for a term of not less
-- than 6 months and has not received a free pardon."
GIVEN `is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN, `has an arrangement with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN, `months of imprisonment sentenced` IS A NUMBER, `received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is disqualified from Board membership` IF
        `is an undischarged bankrupt`
    OR  `has an arrangement with creditors`
    OR  (`months of imprisonment sentenced` AT LEAST 6 AND (NOT `received a free pardon`))

-- Schedule para 8: the office is vacated if the member "(a) has been absent, without leave of the Board, from 3 consecutive meetings
-- of the Board; or (b) becomes in any manner disqualified for membership of the Board."
GIVEN `consecutive meetings missed without leave` IS A NUMBER, `has become disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member's office is vacated` IF
    `consecutive meetings missed without leave` AT LEAST 3 OR `has become disqualified`

-- Schedule para 12(2): "a majority of the members of the Board forms a quorum." (3): a decision "is to be adopted by a simple
-- majority of the members present and voting except that in the case of an equality of votes the Chairperson or member presiding
-- has a casting vote in addition to his or her original vote."
GIVEN `members of the Board` IS A NUMBER, `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a quorum is present` IF
    `members present` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `members of the Board`

GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `the presiding member casts a vote for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the motion is carried` IF
        `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`
    OR  (`votes for` EQUALS `votes against` AND `the presiding member casts a vote for`)
